description: NestJS backend development rules
alwaysApply: false
globs: "apps/api/**/*.ts"
NestJS Backend Rules

Use clear domain boundaries.

Prefer:

module
├── controller
├── service
├── repository
├── dto
├── entities
└── tests


Use dependency injection.

Use DTOs for external input.

Validate external input.

Do not expose database entities directly when doing so leaks internal fields.

Keep controllers thin.

Business logic belongs in services/domain layers.

Do not put business logic into controllers.

Use transactions for multi-step operations requiring atomicity.

Use consistent error handling.

Use consistent API response and pagination conventions.

Do not introduce a new abstraction when an existing project abstraction can be reused.

Before modifying an existing service, inspect its callers.

Do not change public API behavior without checking all consumers.

Backend must remain authoritative for:

prices
inventory
order totals
payments
accounting
commissions
permissions